From: Vertex Shot Timer <vertex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm: dts: infinity6e: stop claiming PAD_GPIO13 for PWM5

The QFN padmux schematic assigns PAD_GPIO13 to PWM5.  drivers/sstar/padmux
applies every schematic entry unconditionally from _mdrv_padmux_dts(), with no
filter for who asked for the pad, so on a board that uses PAD_GPIO13 as the
power-hold line the pad was switched out of GPIO mode and back to PWM5 at
postcore_initcall -- after U-Boot had already driven it high.  The boot log
shows it:

    [Padmux]reset PAD112(reg 0x103c00:d; mask0x8) t0 PWM5_MODE_1 (org: GPIO)

which is exactly the pad being taken away from the board's power latch.

Comment the entry out, the way the pads this board does not use are already
handled in the block above it.  Nothing loses PWM5: DrvPWMPadSet() on
infinity6e is an empty function (its whole body is commented out in
drivers/sstar/pwm/infinity6e/mhal_pwm.c), and the SoC-wide PWM pad-ctrl in
infinity6e.dtsi is all PAD_UNKNOWN to begin with, so PWM5 was only ever being
claimed through this schematic in the first place.

sstar_padmux_resume() replays the same schematic, so removing the entry here
also stops a suspend/resume cycle from re-taking the pad.

Signed-off-by: Vertex Shot Timer <vertex@localhost>
---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/infinity6e-padmux-qfn.dtsi	2026-10-16 16:42:50.991644484 +0700
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/infinity6e-padmux-qfn.dtsi	2026-10-16 16:43:14.618104616 +0700
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@
                 <PAD_GPIO10             PINMUX_FOR_PWM2_MODE_1          MDRV_PUSE_PWM2>,
                 <PAD_GPIO11             PINMUX_FOR_PWM3_MODE_1          MDRV_PUSE_PWM3>,
                 <PAD_GPIO12             PINMUX_FOR_PWM4_MODE_1          MDRV_PUSE_PWM4>,
-                <PAD_GPIO13             PINMUX_FOR_PWM5_MODE_1          MDRV_PUSE_PWM5>,
+                //<PAD_GPIO13             PINMUX_FOR_PWM5_MODE_1          MDRV_PUSE_PWM5>,
                 <PAD_GPIO14             PINMUX_FOR_PWM6_MODE_1          MDRV_PUSE_PWM6>,
                 <PAD_GPIO15             PINMUX_FOR_PWM7_MODE_1          MDRV_PUSE_PWM7>,
                 <PAD_PM_GPIO9           PINMUX_FOR_PWM9_MODE_1          MDRV_PUSE_PWM9>,
